WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.310
"Do you really think Nora took the money?"

2
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:04.650
Cole asked.

3
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.331
"I don't know," Henry said.

4
00:00:06.351 --> 00:00:07.972
"She's just a little kid.

5
00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:14.177
And she has always seemed pretty honest to me.

6
00:00:15.418 --> 00:00:34.203
Remember? She even told the bus driver that his hairpiece looked fake."

7
00:00:35.044 --> 00:00:35.864
Cole laughed.

8
00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:38.727
"I almost forgot about that," he said.

9
00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:41.449
"Good thing the bus driver has a sense of humor!"

10
00:00:43.731 --> 00:00:45.712
Maggie was several steps ahead of them.

11
00:00:46.673 --> 00:00:51.297
She was in such a hurry to reach Nathan and Nora's house that she was almost jogging.

12
00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:52.818
"Hurry up!"

13
00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:54.580
she called over her shoulder.

14
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.384
"I want to get my money back and open up my lemonade stand again."

15
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:03.482
Henry walked a little faster until he caught up with Maggie.

16
00:01:03.502 --> 00:01:08.464
"I wonder why Nora would steal your money," he said.

17
00:01:08.484 --> 00:01:11.746
"She seems pretty young to do something like that."

18
00:01:11.766 --> 00:01:13.307
"That's true."

19
00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.608
Cole had caught up by then too.

20
00:01:15.628 --> 00:01:21.251
"It's hard to believe that Nora suddenly decided to rob Maggie's lemonade stand all by herself."

21
00:01:22.352 --> 00:01:23.192
He looked worried.

22
00:01:23.212 --> 00:01:25.313
"I just thought of something.

23
00:01:26.194 --> 00:01:28.335
What if Nora and Nathan were in cahoots?"

24
00:01:29.375 --> 00:01:30.076
"In cahoots?"

25
00:01:30.452 --> 00:01:31.232
Maggie echoed.

26
00:01:31.252 --> 00:01:33.153
"What the heck does that mean?"

27
00:01:33.173 --> 00:01:37.314
"I heard it on that detective movie I saw on TV," Cole said.

28
00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:41.396
"When someone's in cahoots, it means they're working together."

29
00:01:42.656 --> 00:01:43.437
Henry nodded.

30
00:01:43.457 --> 00:01:45.477
"I see what you mean.

31
00:01:46.558 --> 00:01:52.940
If Nathan and Nora were in cahoots, then Nathan could have distracted Maggie on purpose by talking to

32
00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:58.701
her. He kept her distracted long enough for Nora to grab the money out of the cashbox.

33
00:01:59.682 --> 00:02:03.823
Then once they got away, the two of them could have split the cash between them."

34
00:02:05.243 --> 00:02:06.683
Maggie's eyes widened.

35
00:02:06.703 --> 00:02:09.984
"Do you really think that's what happened?"

36
00:02:10.004 --> 00:02:12.745
"No," Henry said.

37
00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.326
"I don't think Nathan is like that."

38
00:02:15.346 --> 00:02:18.067
"Yeah, I don't either," Cole agreed.

39
00:02:18.087 --> 00:02:20.627
"Maybe it was just Nora after all.

40
00:02:21.487 --> 00:02:23.208
We already know she's a weird kid.

41
00:02:24.604 --> 00:02:27.266
Nathan says she acts sneaky and secretive all the time.

42
00:02:28.226 --> 00:02:29.407
Maybe she's a thief too."

43
00:02:30.527 --> 00:02:35.570
"Maybe." Henry still had a hard time believing Nora was the culprit.

44
00:02:36.471 --> 00:02:41.093
Something was bugging him about the whole situation, though he couldn't figure out what it was.

45
00:02:42.414 --> 00:02:46.536
Then again those teenage girls had seen Nora grab something off the table.

46
00:02:47.417 --> 00:02:49.918
That definitely made the little girl seem guilty.

47
00:02:50.759 --> 00:02:53.100
Besides they were almost out of suspects.

48
00:02:54.172 --> 00:02:57.494
Soon they were turning the corner onto Nathan and Nora's street.

49
00:02:58.414 --> 00:03:02.837
From halfway down the block, they spotted Nora talking and laughing with another girl.

50
00:03:02.857 --> 00:03:07.239
"Looks like Nora has a friend over," Cole commented.

51
00:03:07.259 --> 00:03:10.021
"I don't care," Maggie said.

52
00:03:10.041 --> 00:03:12.422
"I'm going to get my money back."

53
00:03:13.482 --> 00:03:14.443
"Slow down."

54
00:03:14.463 --> 00:03:16.584
Henry grabbed her by the arm.

55
00:03:16.604 --> 00:03:20.846
"You can't just march up to her and demand your money back."

56
00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:22.467
"Oh yeah?

57
00:03:22.927 --> 00:03:23.648
Says who?"

58
00:03:24.084 --> 00:03:24.764
Maggie said.

59
00:03:24.784 --> 00:03:27.845
"Think about it," Henry said.

60
00:03:27.865 --> 00:03:31.466
"We already know that Nora likes to argue.

61
00:03:31.966 --> 00:03:36.388
If you accuse her of being the thief, she'll just argue, whether she did it or not."

62
00:03:36.408 --> 00:03:38.668
"Well, what else can I do?"

63
00:03:39.108 --> 00:03:39.809
asked Maggie.

64
00:03:40.789 --> 00:03:42.789
"She and her friend haven't seen us yet.

65
00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:47.511
Let's hide and spy on them for a little while," Henry suggested.

66
00:03:47.531 --> 00:03:50.131
"Yeah. Like a stakeout!"

67
00:03:51.032 --> 00:03:51.772
Cole grinned.

68
00:03:52.684 --> 00:03:54.785
"The detectives in that mystery movie did that.

69
00:03:55.765 --> 00:03:58.626
They sat in their car in front of a suspect's house all night!"

70
00:03:58.646 --> 00:04:02.067
"I don't want to sit around here all night."

71
00:04:03.007 --> 00:04:05.187
Maggie still sounded a little grumpy.

72
00:04:05.988 --> 00:04:10.089
But she followed the boys as they tiptoed behind a hedge that ran along the side of the

73
00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:13.950
yard. The three of them crouched down behind the hedge.

74
00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:19.451
They could see Nora and her friend through the branches, but the little girls couldn't see them.

75
00:04:19.471 --> 00:04:21.052
"What are they doing?"

76
00:04:21.372 --> 00:04:22.192
Cole whispered.

77
00:04:23.084 --> 00:04:24.866
Henry watched the two little girls.

78
00:04:25.827 --> 00:04:27.768
Nora was holding a stick in one hand.

79
00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.792
The other girl had a crown made of vines on her head.

80
00:04:31.812 --> 00:04:36.216
"It looks like they're playing princesses," Maggie whispered.

81
00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.278
Nora and her friend still didn't see them.

82
00:04:40.219 --> 00:04:43.262
The friend was picking dandelions to weave into her crown.

83
00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:48.266
"I am the prettiest princess in all the land," she said with a giggle.

84
00:04:48.286 --> 00:04:50.148
"So what?

85
00:04:50.844 --> 00:04:53.685
I'm the richest princess in all the world!"

86
00:04:53.885 --> 00:04:54.606
Nora cried.

87
00:04:54.626 --> 00:04:58.788
"I have more jewels than all the other princesses!"

88
00:04:59.528 --> 00:05:01.389
That was all Maggie needed to hear.

89
00:05:01.409 --> 00:05:03.510
"Give it back!"

90
00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.831
she hollered, jumping out from behind the hedge.

91
00:05:06.851 --> 00:05:10.933
"You took what's mine, and I want it back right now!"

92
00:05:12.313 --> 00:05:14.654
Nora and her friend glanced up in surprise.

93
00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:18.236
The friend looked confused—and a little scared.

94
00:05:20.012 --> 00:05:22.136
But Nora instantly burst into tears.

95
00:05:22.156 --> 00:05:24.300
"I'm sorry!"

96
00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:25.382
she sobbed.

97
00:05:25.402 --> 00:05:28.447
"I didn't mean to take it!"
